drm: h713: make dumb buffers fetchable by the video plane

kmssink allocates its buffer pool as dumb buffers and takes every plane's
stride from the pitch dumb_create returns. Stock GStreamer copies frames into
that pool whenever a decoder cannot hand over its own buffers.
v4l2slh265dec does this for every HEVC stream whose SPS has a conformance
crop (copy_frames = need_crop), e.g. 852x480 coded as 856.

The DMA helper's pitch is the tight width (852). AFBD steps strides in whole
16-sample units, so the plane refused the frame and kmssink failed outright
(letterbox Phase 3 gate pre-run, 2026-10-05). Cedrus's own buffers were never
the problem; they are 32-aligned (0125).

  - pitch: 64-byte aligned. That is a multiple of AFBD's 16 samples for
    NV12 and P010, and the alignment Panfrost needs to import a buffer;
  - size: 16 more lines. The plane fetches whole 16x16 blocks, and kmssink
    puts chroma at pitch x height with no padding, so a picture whose height
    is not a multiple of 16 would otherwise be fetched past the object's end.

The console's 1280x720 XRGB framebuffer (pitch 5120) keeps its pitch.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c	2026-10-05 22:42:26.116013797 -0700
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c	2026-10-05 23:09:17.696027293 -0700
@@ -1229,6 +1229,30 @@
 
 DEFINE_DRM_GEM_DMA_FOPS(h713_afbd_fops);
 
+/*
+ * Dumb buffers the video plane can fetch. kmssink allocates its own pool as
+ * dumb buffers and takes every plane's stride from the pitch returned here.
+ * Stock GStreamer copies into that pool whenever a decoder cannot hand its
+ * own buffers over: v4l2slh265dec does it for every HEVC stream with a
+ * conformance crop (852x480 coded as 856). At the helper's tight pitch
+ * (852) AFBD would refuse the frame -- it steps strides in whole 16-sample
+ * units -- and kmssink fails outright.
+ *
+ *  - pitch: 64-byte aligned, a multiple of AFBD's 16 samples for NV12 and
+ *    P010 alike, and the alignment Panfrost needs to import a buffer;
+ *  - size: 16 more lines, so the plane's whole-16x16-block fetch of a
+ *    picture whose height is not a multiple of 16 stays inside the object
+ *    (kmssink puts chroma at pitch x height, with no padding of its own).
+ */
+static int h713_afbd_dumb_create(struct drm_file *file, struct drm_device *drm,
+				 struct drm_mode_create_dumb *args)
+{
+	args->pitch = ALIGN(DIV_ROUND_UP(args->width * args->bpp, 8), 64);
+	args->size = (u64)args->pitch * (args->height + 16);
+
+	return drm_gem_dma_dumb_create_internal(file, drm, args);
+}
+
 static const struct drm_driver h713_afbd_driver = {
 	/*
 	 * DRIVER_RENDER on a display-only device is deliberate and is a
@@ -1253,7 +1277,7 @@
 	.driver_features	= DRIVER_GEM | DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_ATOMIC |
 				  DRIVER_RENDER,
 	.fops			= &h713_afbd_fops,
-	DRM_GEM_DMA_DRIVER_OPS,
+	DRM_GEM_DMA_DRIVER_OPS_WITH_DUMB_CREATE(h713_afbd_dumb_create),
 	DRM_FBDEV_DMA_DRIVER_OPS,
 	.name			= "sun50i-h713-afbd",
 	.desc			= "Allwinner H713 AFBD scanout",
